{
    "summaries": [
        {
            "name": "antique brooch",
            "summary": "Choose a display case made from acid-free materials like wood, glass, or acrylic to prevent damage from acidic substances. Opt for a sturdy frame and a secure closure to prevent the brooch from shifting or falling. Use a soft, padded interior to cushion the brooch and prevent scratching. Select a case with a clear glass or acrylic front for clear visibility and an adjustable display stand or pedestal to showcase the brooch at the perfect angle. Use a removable background or a reversible background with different colors to create a contrasting display. Consider a case with a locking mechanism to prevent unauthorized access or tampering and UV-filtering glass or acrylic to protect the brooch from harmful UV light. If you live in an area with extreme temperatures or humidity, consider a case with climate control features, such as a thermally insulated case or a case with silica gel packets. Choose a finish that complements the brooch's metal, gemstones, or other materials and a finish that complements the era and style of the brooch, whether it's Art Deco, Victorian, or modern. Consider a minimalist or ornate case that lets the brooch take center stage or adds to the overall display."
        }
    ]
}

